.nf
YASMV manual                                                 prove-property

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
prove-property <name> -depth <N> [ -strategy interpolation ] [options]

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Attempt to prove a saved safety property by k-induction, with N from 1 to
10000. Requires a loaded model and a property saved with property set.
A conclusive induction proof checks both base and inductive-step obligations.

-strategy interpolation selects forward interpolation instead. N caps concrete
counterexample search; an invariant can establish an unbounded proof before
that cap. A bounded fallback establishes only the checked depths. The invariant
is verified for initial-state containment, transition closure, and exclusion of
violations. Its circuit, model identity, assumptions, and search statistics are
available through job show -full. Deterministic Boolean state predicates and
one-step transition relations are required; nondeterministic transitions are
supported.

A reachable counterexample is replayed into the native trace register.
An inconclusive inductive step does not establish that the property is false;
its evidence is available through job show -full.

-c <expression> adds an assumption (repeatable). -wall-ms <N> limits computation
time; -conflicts <N> and -propagations <N> limit solver work. -async submits a
background job. Use job wait to retrieve its result or job cancel to cancel it.
Ctrl-C cancels a waiting job. job show -full displays complete evidence.
Shell options use one dash; -- starts an SMV comment.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> property set once !DUPLICATE
>> prove-property once -depth 12
>> prove-property once -strategy interpolation -depth 12
>> job show -full

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help property, help check-property, help job.
